Spec: Explicit authenticated server command

Purpose:
  Run the real device-authorized control and FRP listeners using protected persistent Linux state.

Owns:
  ./main.go
  ./main_test.go

References:
  /control-plane/serverhost/serverhost.sdd
  /backend-frp/overlays/server/linkgate.sdd

Must:
  Keep initialization separate from serving and require an explicit protected configuration path for either command.
  An explicit identity-request command requires a protected directory and creates only a host-local key and public CSR; it does not issue trust or modify authority.
  Never generate an owner key, bootstrap on ordinary startup, reuse fixture grants or open stock FRP admission after an error.
  Bind only the two configured listeners; no dashboard, public proxy, UDP listener or implicit STUN service is enabled.
  Stop both listeners and authority on shutdown, storage identity failure or an unexpected listener exit, before closing databases.
  Emit only fixed aggregate readiness/errors and suppress raw upstream logs that could reflect network candidates or runtime input.
  Initialization and serving remain local commands without service installation, cloud mutation or deployment side effects.
